      "successfulRequestCount": 0,
      "loggedRequestAttempts": 0,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 0,
      "outputTokens": 0,
      "costUsd": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "So space the values by their powers of ten instead. Ten to the three bytes goes at three, ten to the six at six, and so on. That's taking log base ten of each value. Now every step along the axis means multiplying by ten, because log of ten times ay number is one more than the log of the number. Equal steps mean equal factors, not equal differences. That's a logarithmic scale. Kilobyte, megabyte, gigabyte and terabyte sit three steps apart, and every file has its own place."
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-04",
      "changed": true,
      "audio": "public/audio/math-a12-t04/scene-04.wav",
      "durationInFrames": 1096,
