      "inputTokens": 0,
      "outputTokens": 0,
      "costUsd": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "For dilute solutions, pH is minus log base ten of the hydrogen ion concentration, so more hydrogen ions mean a lower pH. Each step of one is a factor of ten. A solution at pH four has ten to the minus four moles per litre, and pH seven has ten to the minus seven. So pH four has a thousand times the hydrogen ion concentration, even though the numbers differ by only three."
    },
