      "pronunciationText": "Star magnitudes have a minus sign and a two point five. The difference in magnitudes is minus two point five times log of the brightness ratio. So brighter stars get smaller magnitudes, and five magnitudes is a factor of ten to the two, a hundred. A magnitude one star is a hundred times as bright as a magnitude six star."
    },
